Why document.getElementById('keywords') instead of ref drilling:
When threading the ref through HotelTypeaheadInput → TypeaheadInput → IconTextInput, the ref was being spread into ...props and passed down to underlying elements, which conflicted with react-hook-form's internal ref used for form registration. This caused the search form submit to stop working.
The fix would have required a mergeRefs utility to combine both refs, adding complexity to shared base components (TypeaheadInput, HotelTypeaheadInput) that have no other need for this.
Since IconTextInput already has id="keywords" hardcoded as a stable identifier, using document.getElementById was the safer and simpler tradeoff — it avoids touching shared components and doesn't risk breaking form submission behavior.
